// rl/ — reinforcement learning: recurrent policies, actors and critics.
//
// One package rather than several, and that is a measured decision rather than
// a convenient one. The recurrent architectures call each other constantly --
// gru_cell reaches into lstm_cell 39 times, the RL update code reaches back
// into lstm_cell 18, lstm_cell's own wrappers are used by the SAC agents --
// so splitting "recurrent" from "rl" would produce an import cycle between two
// packages that are each half of the same idea.
//
// The Decision Transformer and Trajectory Transformer live here too. They are
// offline-RL methods that happen to be built on an LSTM cell rather than a
// transformer, and they are mutually entangled with it: decision_transformer
// needs lstm_cell and gtrxl_block, trajectory_transformer needs the same, and
// both bring their own buffers (dt_embeddings, beam_search_planner, n_step_buffer,
// trajectory_buffer) that nothing outside this package uses.
//
// Depends on core, nn and optim. The GRU/LSTM cells are matrix arithmetic; the
// critics and Q-networks are LinearParam plus the activ ops; and the trainers
// step their parameters through an optimizer, which is optim/'s whole job.
//
// optim/ used to point back at nn/, which made this cycle until sqrtf moved
// down to core/. The direction is now one-way: rl -> optim -> nn.
import {
  "moonbitlang/core/math",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/core",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/nn",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/activ",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/optim",
}
